## Question (from the maintainer)
"Review homeassistant util and helper modules to see if there's something else we recreated instead of using a built-in."

The trigger: we had written our own fake clock class for rate-limit tests, when HA's test harness already provides `freezer` (freezegun). HA's `pytest_homeassistant_custom_component` plugin even routes the event-loop clock through `time.monotonic` (`patch_time.py`, `runner.monotonic`).

## Scope
- **LCM code:** read `custom_components/lock_code_manager/` (production) and `tests/` (test helpers, fixtures, `tests/common.py`, `conftest.py` files). Code on `origin/main` is current; use the main checkout, which tracks main.
